{"type":"message","id":"be9531b5","parentId":"98c59cf6","timestamp":"2026-05-18T17:47:29.884Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Same error. Let me try with \"messageId\" field, or maybe there's a different auth header needed. Let me check if the API expects a different auth method. The fact that GET works with X-API-Key but POST doesn't is strange.\n\nLet me try with \"Authorization: Bearer\" since that's what was first tried.\n\nActually wait - when I used \"Authorization: Bearer\" I got \"Unauthorized\". When I used \"X-API-Key\" the GET worked. But POST still fails with 1101.\n\nError 1101 in Cloudflare Workers typically means \"Worker exceeded CPU time\" or similar. But that's unlikely here.\n\nMaybe the POST endpoint doesn't exist or the path is different. Let me try different paths.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-f98ae2f4-8913-47ce-8058-c5f149a01eeb","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"thread\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"test\"}' \\\n  \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\""}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-609deede-9316-42c2-a427-5b2267c2d5b7","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{}' \\\n  \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":301,"output":311,"cacheRead":19440,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20052,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779126439397,"responseId":"chatcmpl-0c567f13-3e30-4963-836f-a9869cb45c56"}}
