{"type":"message","id":"f9bcb923","parentId":"465d29b2","timestamp":"2026-05-18T17:47:52.598Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Error 1101 is a Cloudflare Workers error - typically \"Worker exceeded memory\" or a similar runtime error. This seems to indicate the `/send` endpoint exists but is crashing when it receives our request. The error is happening on the server side, not a validation failure.\n\nThis could be because:\n1. The request body format is wrong\n2. The endpoint is buggy\n3. There's some server-side validation we're not aware of\n\nLet me try sending just a minimal valid request to see if it's a body parsing issue.\n\nActually, let me try GET with different parameters to see if there's a /message or /post endpoint.\n\nWait - error 1101 is a specific error code in Cloudflare Workers. It typically means the worker threw an uncaught exception or exceeded resources. \n\nThe POST endpoint seems to have a server-side bug. Let me try a few different content formats.\n\nActually, looking at this from a different angle - maybe error 1101 is the API's own error code, not the Cloudflare HTTP status. The response body is literally \"error code: 1101\" which looks like JSON.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-b53ca791-7295-4236-917d-ad1034e4d7a3","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: text/plain\" \\\n  -d 'hello' \\\n  \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\""}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-79350906-46eb-4866-8a74-92e4ea68a388","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X GET -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send?threadId=arbitration&content=test\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":807,"output":374,"cacheRead":19280,"c